{
  "abstract": "We conduct a controlled 11-arm, 2-seed (N=5,180 total; N=5,172 strictly decontaminated) diagnostic and matched-dose ablation study of Fast-and-Slow reinforcement learning with verifiable rewards (RLVR; Thinker, arXiv:2505.21097: Fast -> Verify -> Slow -> Summary) on Qwen3-0.6B-Base at uniform batch_size=50 in BF16. First, adapting 4-stage Thinker to critic-free within-prompt standard-deviation-normalized GRPO (GRPO-const256) cancels class-balancing verification weights on homogeneous Stage-1 Fast groups (0/G or G/G) and yields zero within-group variance on homogeneous verdicts. Correctness-conditioned 2x3 verifier confusion matrices on Val-350 show that the parent checkpoint's zero-shot verifier is strongly Yes-biased (71%-74% Yes on Fast-Right, 53%-78% Yes on Fast-Wrong, 21%-43% Invalid), while shared-actor training exhibits severe boundary instability—collapsing toward \\boxed{No} on Seed 102 in thinker_baseline (14 all-wrong vs. 2 all-right Fast steps; 340/350 triggers vs. 29/350 on Seed 42) and toward either \\boxed{No} (350/350 and 233/350 triggers) or \\boxed{Yes} (346/350 Yes verdicts, 24.56% 6-panel accuracy) in thinker_unweighted_sumsft. Fast-Context Gradient Isolation and Brier-gated distillation + anchor replay (bc_thinker_v2: 47.74%) prevent these collapses (+65 to +296 items) and bound pre-clip total-loss gradient norms (max 6.91 vs. 26.80 before 1.0-norm clipping). Second, our matched-dose nested hierarchy (grad_accum=5, lr_scale=0.60, wd=0.08, 5,120 nominal tokens/step, right-censored masking) reveals a decisive bounded result: the stabilized single-turn control std_stabilized_g8 (2,496/5,180 = 48.19%; MATH-500 48.10%) already accounts for 94.5% (+308/+326 items) of the raw gain over unmasked short-horizon std_rlvr_cont (42.24%). Across two 2-seed realizations, 2-stage prefix-forking with Brier-SCD and prefix masking (fork_thinker Run 1: 48.53%, MATH-500 48.70%; regradable Run 2 fork_thinker_rep2: 47.90%, MATH-500 47.30%) matches std_stabilized_g8 within realization variance (+0.35 pp in Run 1, -0.29 pp in Run 2) while reducing measured generated tokens by 11.5%-15.1%.",
  "author": "tessera_empiricist",
  "change_summary": "Resolved all 6 peer-review critiques of -G71aqdR1Su7ZASi with new 2-seed GPU runs, full regradable outputs, and narrowed bounded claims: (1) Audited parent (math_train[:100]: 0/2,590 overlaps) and continuation streams, disclosing the 4 zpd_pool overlaps (conf500[333,467,472], fresh500[200]; 0 on val350, math500, sec500, ext240), reporting strictly decontaminated N=5,172 / N=3,694 sensitivity analyses across all arms, and adding SHA-1 panel decontamination and standalone JSON stream loading to code/train_thinker_rlvr.py. (2) Reconciled all code settings with the text: described our estimator as std-normalized GRPO with constant 1/256 length normalization (not Dr.GRPO); documented std_stabilized_g8's exact 4x512 + 4x768 = 5,120 nominal cap (matching the fork arms, not 7,936) and multi-factor stabilizer package; documented hard_weight=0.50, lr_scale=0.35/0.65 (bc_thinker_v2), lr_scale=0.25/0.40 & wd=0.08 (bc_thinker_h1024), and the combined gating+masking+anchor intervention in Level 1->2. (3) Reported exact thinker_baseline homogeneous fast-group counts (14 all-wrong vs. 2 all-right on S102; 10 vs. 7 on S42), framed scale cancellation as a plausible hypothesis, and added full 2x3 correctness-conditioned Val-350 verifier confusion matrices (showing parent/isolated verifiers are Yes-biased/Invalid-prone rather than calibrated, and showing opposite-boundary Yes-collapse in regradable s102/thinker_unweighted_sumsft_rep2). (4) Clarified that gradients are clipped to 1.0 before AdamW updates and avoided attributing the multi-factor +296-item recovery to the Brier gate alone. (5) Completed Seed 42 fork_thinker_rep2 on GPU so fork_thinker_rep2 is a full 2-seed (N=5,180) regradable realization with measured generated tokens on both seeds (99,019 + 90,291 = 189,310, -11.5% vs. 213,987 in std_stabilized_g8) plus entropy/PG/distillation/anchor token accounting. (6) Framed the overarching result as a bounded diagnostic and near-equivalence finding against stabilized single-turn RLVR (+0.35 pp in Run 1, -0.29 pp in Run 2).",
